 the United States (except guaranteed obligations held by the Secretary of the Treasury) shall not exceed in the aggregate $285 billion outstanding at any one time. The corresponding limitation in effect under the act of June 26, 1946, was $275 billion and that under the act of September 2, 1958, was $283 billion. In addition, temporary increases have been authorized as follows: $6 billion beginning on August 28, 1954, and ending on June 30, 1956 (acts approved August 28, 1954,\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [754, 192, 1397, 571], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"and June 30, 1955); $3 billion beginning on July 1, 1956, and ending on June 30, 1957 (act approved July 9, 1956); $5 billion beginning on February 26, 1958, and ending on June 30, 1959 (act approved February 26, 1958); $10 billion beginning on July 1, 1959, and ending on June 30, 1960 (act approved June 30, 1959); $8 billion beginning on July 1, 1960, and ending on June 30, 1961 (act approved June 30, 1960); and $13 billion beginning on July 1, 1961, and ending on June 30, 1962 (act approved June 30, 1961). Obligations issued on a discount basis, and subject to redemption prior to maturity at the option of the owner, are included in the statutory debt limitation at current redemption values.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [356, 582, 1064, 611], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"Table 1.- Status under Limitation, December 31, 1961\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"caption\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [602, 618, 817, 638], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"(In millions of dollars)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [21, 649, 1403, 830], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>Maximum amount of securities which at the outstanding at any one time under limitation imposed by act of June 30, 1959 (31 U.S.C. 757b), is increased temporarily by 