961-December: Treasury notes of 1890 = 2,120\n\nI notice the values fluctuate between $2,094 million and $2,120 million throughout 1961. The asterisk suggests a significant reduction, potentially to less than $500,000 in fiscal year 1962. This indicates a potential complete retirement of these notes during that period.\n\nThe footnotes reveal a critical insight: in October 1961, $1 million in Treasury notes of 1890 were destroyed, marking the beginning of their removal from government ledgers. This suggests 1961 might be the pivotal year for their elimination.\n\nI'm investigating whether the Treasury notes were entirely removed in 1961 or 1962, focusing on the precise timeline of their retirement. The data hints at a transition point during these years.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_2bdd1b085c9a42b0912c10ef","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nimport json\nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1962_01.json') as f:\n    data = json.load(f)\n# Find the table with Treasury notes of 1890\ndoc = data['document']\nfor elem in doc['elements']:\n    if elem.get('type') == 'table' and elem.get('name'):\n        if 'Treasury notes of 1890' in str(elem.get('name', '')):\n            print('Found table:', elem.get('name'))\n            print('Rows:', len(elem.get('rows', [])))\n\""}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
