recise increase in paper money circulation for 1962. By tracking the values from January through November, I can determine the net addition to paper money during that calendar year. The key is to find the exact difference between the start and end points of 1962's paper money circulation.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_8458aeb4d57d4ddbbc641d3b","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nimport re\n\n# Read the 1963 page 88 file \nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1963_01_page_88.txt', 'r') as f:\n    content = f.read()\n\n# Find monthly data for 1962 - extract paper money values\n# Looking for patterns like '1962-January', '1962-February', etc.\nrows = re.findall(r'<tr><td>(.*?)</td><td>(.*?)</td><td>(.*?)</td><td>(.*?)</td><td>(.*?)</td><td>(.*?)</td><td>(.*?)</td><td>(.*?)</td><td>(.*?)</td><td>(.*?)</td></tr>', content)\n\nprint('Looking for 1962 monthly data:')\nfor row in rows:\n    if '1962' in row[0] or ('January' in row[0] and len(row[0]) < 20) or ('February' in row[0] and len(row[0]) < 20) or ('March' in row[0] and len(row[0]) < 20) or ('April' in row[0] and len(row[0]) < 20) or ('May' in row[0] and len(row[0]) < 20) or ('June' in row[0] and len(row[0]) < 20) or ('July' in row[0] and len(row[0]) < 20) or ('August' in row[0] and len(row[0]) < 20) or ('September' in row[0] and len(row[0]) < 20) or ('October' in row[0] and len(row[0]) < 20) or ('November' in row[0] and len(row[0]) < 20) or ('December' in row[0] and len(row[0]) < 20):\n        if '1961' not in row[0] and '1960' not in row[0] and '195' not in row[0]:\n            print(f'{row[0]} | Paper: {row[2]}')\n\""}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
