{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775333126-1qPsc8WUkYzOT8es7yGp","role":"assistant","created":1775333139,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I need to calculate the paper money added in circulation during calendar year 1961. The question asks about \"how much paper money was added in circulation\" in the year when Treasury notes of 1890 were removed from the ledgers.\n\nLooking at the data:\n- January 1961: Paper money = $29,385 million\n- December 1961: Paper money = $30,442 million (from December 1960-December data, or $30,975 from November 1961)\n\nActually wait - looking at the data more carefully:\n- June 1961: Paper money = $29,943 million  \n- December 1960: Paper money = $30,442 million\n- November 1961: Paper money = $30,975 million\n\nHmm, this is confusing. Let me look more carefully at the data flow within 1961. Looking at the table:\n\n1960-December: 30,442\n1961-January: 29,385\n...\n1961-June: 29,943 (end of fiscal year 1961)\n1961-December: 30,442 (or 30,975 in November)\n\nWait, looking at the earlier search output, the 1961-December data shows Paper money = 30,442. But I need to check this more carefully.\n\nActually, looking at the first result again:\n- 1961-January: Paper money = 29,385\n- November 1961: Paper money = 30,975\n\nSo the change from January 1961 to November 1961 would be: 30,975 - 29,385 = 1,590 million\n\nOr from December 1960 to November 1961: 30,975 - 30,442 = 533 million\n\nLet me re-examine the table data more carefully. Actually, looking at the tables:\n\nFrom 1962 bulletin page 82:\n- 1960-December: Paper money 30,442\n- 1961-January: Paper money 29,385\n\n\n- November 1961: Paper money shows 30,975, but December 1961 drops to 30,442.\n\nI realize now the data is from two different Treasury Bulletins. The 1962 bulletin shows December 1961 data, while the 1963 bulletin provides November 1961 details. This explains the discrepancy in the figures.\n\nExamining the Treasury Bulletin 1963's page 88 data reveals a key insight: fiscal year 1962 shows an asterisk for Treasury notes of 1890, indicating less than $500,000 - effectively zero. The removal happened during 1961, specifically on October 20, 1961, when $1 million in notes was determined to be destroyed or lost. \n\nThe calendar year 1961 saw the formal recognition of these notes' removal from government ledgers. Analyzing the paper money data, I find the change from December 1960 to December 1961 is 0 million. However, the January to November 1961 data shows an increase of 1,590 million, which seems more representative of the actual paper money circulation during that period.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_7f29227e306e4c62b3997f12","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 -c \"\n# Looking at the 1962 page 82 data more carefully\n# Let me parse the table properly\n\nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1962_01_page_82.txt', 'r') as f:\n    content = f.read()\n\nimport re\n# Extract rows with paper money data\n# Looking at the pattern for monthly data\n\n# The pattern should capture month data\nrows = re.findall(r'<tr><td>([^<]+)</td><td>([^<]*)</td><td>([^<]*)</td><td>([^<]*)</td><td>([^<]*)</td><td>([^<]*)</td><td>([^<]*)</td><td>([^<]*)</td><td>([^<]*)</td><td>([^<]*)</td></tr>', content)\n\n# Filter for 1961 months and 1960-December\nprint('Date               | Total  | Paper  | T1890')\nprint('-' * 55)\nfor row in rows:\n    date = row[0].strip()\n    # Look for December 1960, and all months in 1961\n    if date == '1960-December' or (date.startswith('1961-') or (date in ['January', 'February', 'March', 'April', 'May', 'June', 'July', 'August', 'September', 'October', 'November'] and '1962' not in date and '1960' not in date)):\n        # Only print paper money rows (not coin)\n        if 'Total money' not in row[1] and row[1]:\n            try:\n                # Clean up the paper money value\n                paper = row[2].replace(',', '').strip()\n                if paper and paper != 'Total coin':\n                    print(f'{date:18} | {row[1]:6} | {row[2]:6} | {row[4]}')\n            except:\n                pass\n\""}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
