efully:\n# The table shows:\n# 1962 | 33,770 | 31,117 | 29 | 2,009 | * | 318 | 28,622 | 85 | 53\n\n# That's fiscal year 1962 - Treasury 1890 = 2,009, US notes = *\n# But wait, I misread. Let me check the columns again\nprint('Checking columns in the table...')\n\n# Looking at the header: \n# Total paper money, Gold certificates, Silver certificates, Treasury notes of 1890, United States notes, etc.\n# So the columns are:\n# Date | Total | Total Paper | Gold | Silver | T1890 | USNotes | FRNotes | FRBNotes | NBNotes\n\""}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
