o (*), which supports 1961 as the removal year. The increase in paper money from December 1960 to December 1961 was 894 million dollars.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_7d03afce78cc42b4b02b2c24","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 -c \"\n# Let me verify the question is about paper money added, not total money\n\n# The question asks: 'how much paper money was added in circulation?'\n\n# From the data:\n# December 1960: Paper money = 30,442 million\n# December 1961: Paper money = 31,336 million\n\n# So in calendar year 1961, paper money added = 31,336 - 30,442 = 894 million\n\nprint('Answer: The treasury notes of 1890 were removed from the ledgers in 1961')\nprint('Paper money added in circulation in 1961:')\nprint('December 1960:', 30442, 'million')\nprint('December 1961:', 31336, 'million')\nprint('Increase (paper money added):', 31336 - 30442, 'million dollars')\n\""}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
