uation. The Treasury determined in October 1961 that $1 million of these notes were destroyed, but the data suggests a more dramatic reduction. The monthly progression from $2,098 million in November 1961 to essentially zero by December 1961 indicates a significant write-off or removal of these notes from circulation during that specific period.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_c9abac4c9fd9419badb74d19","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 -c \"\n# Let me verify my interpretation - I need to check the exact values for Treasury notes of 1890\n# in Dec 1960 and Dec 1961 to confirm when they went to *\n\n# From 1962 bulletin page 82:\n# December 1960: <td>1960-December</td><td>32,869</td><td>30,442</td><td>30</td><td>2,110</td><td>1</td>...\n# The columns would be: Date, Total, Paper, Gold, Silver, T1890, USNotes...\n# So T1890 = 1 (million)\n\n# From 1963 bulletin page 88:\n# December 1961: <td>1961-December</td><td>33,918</td><td>31,336</td><td>30</td><td>2,120</td><td>*</td>...\n# T1890 = * (less than $500,000)\n\n# So Treasury notes went from 1 million in Dec 1960 to effectively 0 in Dec 1961\n\n# Let me look at this more carefully - is the 1 in Dec 1960 the actual value?\n# Looking at the 1962 table structure again...\n\n# Actually I think I had the columns wrong. Let me trace through more carefully.\n# From 1963 page 88 header: \n# 'Total money in circulation' | 'Paper money' with sub-columns: Total, Gold, Silver, Treasury 1890, US Notes, etc.\n\n# Let me extract the exact string for Dec 1961 line\nimport re\nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1963_01_page_88.txt', 'r') as f:\n    content = f.read()\n    \n# Find the exact row\nmatch = re.search(r'<tr><td>1961-December</td>(.*?)</tr>', content, re.DOTALL)\nif match:\n    print('Dec 1961 row:', match.group(1)[:200])\n\""}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
